To read all lines of a file asynchronously in C#, you can use the `StreamReader` class along with the `ReadLineAsync` method. This method allows you to read lines of text from a stream asynchronously, which is particularly useful for handling large files or when you need to process the lines concurrently.

Here's a sample method that reads all lines of a file asynchronously:

```csharp
using System;
using System.IO;
using System.Threading.Tasks;

public class FileReader
{
    public async Task<string[]> ReadAllLinesAsync(string filePath)
    {
        using (var reader = new StreamReader(filePath))
        {
            var lines = new List<string>();
            while (!reader.EndOfStream)
            {
                lines.Add(await reader.ReadLineAsync());
            }
            return lines.ToArray();
        }
    }
}

// Example usage:
public class Program
{
    public static async Task Main(string[] args)
    {
        var fileReader = new FileReader();
        string filePath = "path/to/your/file.txt";
        string[] lines = await fileReader.ReadAllLinesAsync(filePath);

        foreach (var line in lines)
        {
            Console.WriteLine(line);
        }
    }
}
```

